Maybe Monica used to use them with--

270
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:21,290
Don't say Richard.

271
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,400
Well, if they're not Monica's

272
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:26,310
and they're not yours, then whose are they?

273
00:13:26,310 --> 00:13:27,560
I think you're forgetting

274
00:13:27,560 --> 00:13:30,670
the kinkiest former resident of that room.

275
00:13:30,670 --> 00:13:32,820
- Pheebs! - Yeah!

276
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:37,170
I think these are yours.

277
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:42,880
These are not mine. Look how flimsy they are. Come on.

278
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:47,570
My God, you try to hang a guy from a water pipe with these...

279
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:50,160
...they'll snap like a piece of licorice.

280
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:54,200
- Can I talk to you alone for a minute? - Sure.

281
00:13:57,490 --> 00:14:01,230
You don't really handcuff guys to water pipes do you?

282
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:04,020
Where do you think Mike really is?

283
00:14:13,130 --> 00:14:14,870
Oh, honey....

284
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,340
Let me just saying something

285
00:14:16,340 --> 00:14:17,630
because once we get into this...

286
00:14:17,630 --> 00:14:18,950
...I'm gonna get all uncomfortable

287
00:14:18,950 --> 00:14:21,630
and probably make some stupid joke.

288
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,250
I just want to say that l-- I love you.

289
00:14:28,770 --> 00:14:31,050
And I'm gonna miss you.

290
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:34,450
And I'm so sad that you're leaving.

291
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:39,280
Oh, you know what?

292
00:14:40,550 --> 00:14:42,890
Let's not say anything else.

293
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,690
I love you.

294
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:48,460
Not so tight.

295
00:14:52,050 --> 00:14:53,450
I'm sorry, give me one more chance.

296
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:54,060
Okay.

297
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,380
Okay.

298
00:14:57,560 --> 00:15:01,420
I'm sorry. Just go. Just go. I can't. I can't.

299
00:15:07,610 --> 00:15:09,600
So I guess you're next. You ready?

300
00:15:09,610 --> 00:15:10,640
I don't think so.

301
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:12,320
Oh, you're definitely not.

302
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,340
I haven't cried like that in years.

303
00:15:14,340 --> 00:15:16,860
You cried yesterday at the 6:00 news.

304
00:15:16,860 --> 00:15:20,640
That old woman was being scammed by her mechanic.

305
00:15:21,850 --> 00:15:25,050
God, I can't believe she saved me for last.

306
00:15:25,050 --> 00:15:26,890
Why are they taking so long?

307
00:15:26,890 --> 00:15:27,630
I don't know.

308
00:15:27,630 --> 00:15:31,320
But, God, Joey seems to be handling it surprisingly well.

309
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:37,200
- No! - No! Joey!

310
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:47,090
Okay, here we go.

311
00:15:48,190 --> 00:15:53,170
- Well.... - Yeah.

312
00:15:54,210 --> 00:15:56,300
I think I'm gonna take off.

313
00:16:01,090 --> 00:16:03,830
Oh, you guys, this was an amazing night.

314
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:05,440
Thank you so much.

315
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:07,000
I love you.

316
00:16:07,210 --> 00:16:08,710
Good night.

317
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:14,460
What?!

318
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:20,000
I don't get a goodbye?

319
00:16:20,140 --> 00:16:21,840
Lucky bastard.

320
00:16:29,560 --> 00:16:30,800
Unbelievable.

321
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,090
She says goodbye to everyone but me!

322
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:35,540
Well, maybe she thought that with all of your history,

323
00:16:35,540 --> 00:16:36,790
it could be...

324
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:38,130
...you know, implicit.

325
00:16:38,130 --> 00:16:40,990
Well, it needs to be "plicit."

326
00:16:41,410 --> 00:16:42,740
All right, let's think about this.

327
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:44,750
I mean, there's gotta be an explanation.

328
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:47,200
Did you do anything to make her mad?

329
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,120
No, I don't think so.

330
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:53,150
You know, maybe she was just really spent from our talk.

331
00:16:53,150 --> 00:16:54,970
- It was pretty intense. - Yeah, mine too.

332
00:16:54,970 --> 00:16:57,530
- Mine was a humdinger. - Okay!

333
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:00,580
I mean, don't I deserve anything?

334
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:05,010
I mean, a few tears, a cursory hug?

335
00:17:06,450 --> 00:17:08,580
Not from you!

336
00:17:09,780 --> 00:17:11,230
Ross, if you're this upset,

337
00:17:11,230 --> 00:17:12,920
you should go and talk to her.

338
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,440
And say what? You owe me a goodbye?

339
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:17,600
I mean, he's got more pride than that.

340
00:17:17,600 --> 00:17:19,510
The hell I do!

341
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:25,430
- I don't get a goodbye? - What?

342
00:17:25,430 --> 00:17:27,750
Everyone gets a goodbye but me?

343
00:17:27,750 --> 00:17:30,010
What do I gotta do to get a goodbye?

344
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:33,150
Be best friends with you? Go out with you?

345
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:34,580
Have a baby with you?

346
00:17:34,580 --> 00:17:35,410
Oh, wait a minute. Wait a minute!

347
00:17:35,410 --> 00:17:37,410
I did all those things!

348
00:17:38,530 --> 00:17:39,040
Ross--

349
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:40,780
Or maybe I'm just not giving you...

350
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:41,820
...enough credit.

351
00:17:41,820 --> 00:17:45,730
I mean, it is difficult to say goodbye to five people.

352
00:17:45,730 --> 00:17:48,720
Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye, goodbye, g--

353
00:17:48,720 --> 00:17:50,900
It's physically impossible!

354
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:54,160
You know what?

355
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:56,240
After all we've been through...

356
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,880
...l can't believe this is

357
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:59,600
how you want to leave things between us.

358
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,250
Have a good time in Paris.

359
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,160
I hope Ross isn't too upset.

360
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,540
I'm sure he's not more bummed out...

361
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:12,400
- ...than I am. - Tell me about it.

362
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,210
Well, you can't say

363
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:15,270
we don't know how to throw a party.

364
00:18:16,490 --> 00:18:18,800
I think I'm gonna head out.

365
00:18:19,530 --> 00:18:20,930
Where do you think you're going?

366
00:18:20,930 --> 00:18:22,750
I thought I was going home to bed...

367
00:18:22,750 --> 00:18:23,970
...but I'm sensing

368
00:18:23,970 --> 00:18:26,630
there's something less fun for me to do here.

369
00:18:27,710 --> 00:18:28,930
We're moving in a couple of days,

370
00:18:28,930 --> 00:18:30,500
and we got a lot of packing to do.

371
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,300
It'd be great if you guys could pitch in.

372
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:34,450
Joey and I can finish up the guest room.

373
00:18:34,450 --> 00:18:36,220
Yeah, good idea.

374
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:41,100
Oh, no. You and Phoebe are gonna help me in here.

375
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,470
You couldn't be cool.

376
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:46,680
We're gonna start in the kitchen.

377
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,370
Plates get put into plate protectors

378
00:18:48,370 --> 00:18:49,960
and stacked 10 to a box.

379
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,910
The silverware gets bundled in rubber bands

380
00:18:51,910 --> 00:18:54,010
and then bubble wrapped. Got it?

381
00:18:54,010 --> 00:18:54,550
Yeah.

382
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:56,190
Good. I need you to be careful...

383
00:18:56,190 --> 00:18:58,910
...and efficient. And remember, if I'm harsh with you...

384
00:18:58,910 --> 00:19:01,810
...it is only because you're doing it wrong.

385
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:07,060
Hey, Mon, I think I figured out whose handcuffs they are.

386
00:19:07,060 --> 00:19:08,160
You did? How?

387
00:19:08,170 --> 00:19:09,780
Well, I was cleaning out the closet...

388
00:19:09,790 --> 00:19:12,140
...and I found some pictures of them...

389
00:19:12,670 --> 00:19:16,340
- ...being used. - Oh, my God, let me see.

390
00:19:18,350 --> 00:19:20,280
Who's that dirty old lady?

391
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:23,130
Monica's grandmother.

392
00:19:25,200 --> 00:19:27,710
Nana liked it rough!

393
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,300
- Hi. - Hey.

394
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:32,670
- Oh, here, have a seat. - Yeah.

395
00:19:32,670 --> 00:19:34,950
- How was your night? - Oh, it was okay.

396
00:19:34,950 --> 00:19:36,380
I went to a movie with my cousin

397
00:19:36,380 --> 00:19:37,740
then out for dinner.

398
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,990
We went to this place that had--

399
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:49,760
Anyway, they had these really amazing cheeseburgers.

400
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:53,710
Erica, are you okay?

401
00:19:53,710 --> 00:19:55,570
Yeah, you know, maybe I ate too much.

402
00:19:55,570 --> 00:19:57,540
I keep getting these stomachaches.

403
00:19:57,540 --> 00:20:00,480
They come and go every few minutes.

404
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:02,990
Oh, my God.

405
00:20:02,990 --> 00:20:06,040
Relax, we'll just get her some antacids.

406
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:09,380
She doesn't have a stomachache! She's in labor!

407
00:20:09,380 --> 00:20:10,360
Oh, my God!

408
00:20:10,370 --> 00:20:12,190
Yeah, you gotta get to the hospital!

409
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,320
Chandler, get the coats! Erica, let's go!

410
00:20:14,320 --> 00:20:16,390
Phoebe and Joey, keep packing!

411
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:18,420
Oh, my God, we're gonna have a baby.

412
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:21,570
We're gonna have a baby!

413
00:20:21,570 --> 00:20:23,820
Oh, my God, we're gonna have a baby!

414
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:25,260
Oh, God, I've gotta sit down!

415
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,830
I've gotta sit down!

416
00:20:28,780 --> 00:20:29,940
Honey, it's gonna be okay.

417
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:32,650
You can do this. Just breathe.

418
00:20:32,650 --> 00:20:35,370
Okay. Okay.

419
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:37,830
Okay, I feel a little better.

420
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:40,220
Are you sure?

421
00:20:41,540 --> 00:20:43,810
Yes, I'm sure. Oh, honey, let's go.

422
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:44,610
Okay.

423
00:20:44,610 --> 00:20:45,650
Okay, bye, everyone!

424
00:20:45,650 --> 00:20:48,020
- We're having a baby! - Good luck!

425
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:49,900
- Chandler, wait, wait, wait! - What?

426
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:50,810
If you get a second,

427
00:20:50,810 --> 00:20:53,370
find out where she got that cheeseburger.

428
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:02,610
You think I didn't say goodbye to you

429
00:21:02,610 --> 00:21:04,340
because I don't care?

430
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:06,020
That's what it seemed like.

431
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:08,470
I cannot believe that after 10 years

432
00:21:08,470 --> 00:21:10,670
you do not know one thing about me!

433
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:12,650
Then why didn't you say something?

434
00:21:12,650 --> 00:21:16,260
Because it is too damn hard, Ross!

435
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:19,090
I can't even begin to explain to you

436
00:21:19,090 --> 00:21:21,300
how much I am gonna miss you.

437
00:21:21,660 --> 00:21:23,550
When I think about not seeing you every day,

438
00:21:23,550 --> 00:21:26,340
it makes me not want to go.

439
00:21:26,940 --> 00:21:28,900
Okay? So if you think that

440
00:21:28,900 --> 00:21:30,120
I didn't say goodbye to you...

441
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,720
...because you don't mean as much to me

442
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:33,880
as everybody else, you're wrong.

443
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:36,300
It's because you mean more to me.

444
00:21:36,890 --> 00:21:39,750
So there, all right? There's your goodbye!

445
00:21:39,860 --> 00:21:41,230
- Rach! - What?

446
00:21:41,230 --> 00:21:44,010
- You keep-- You can't-- - What?

447
00:22:05,870 --> 00:22:07,680
- A little more. - Okay.

448
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:12,120
- A little more. A little more. - All right.

449
00:22:12,830 --> 00:22:14,760
Little more.

450
00:22:17,290 --> 00:22:19,220
All right. All right, let's do this.

451
00:22:19,230 --> 00:22:19,900
All right, ready?

452
00:22:19,900 --> 00:22:23,320
Yep. Now give me your best shot.

453
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:25,400
All right. Here goes.

454
00:22:31,100 --> 00:22:32,820
Doesn't work.

